(5102453, 741110, 37673, '<td valign="top">Composition;<br/> A slight shift to the right would have done a bit of good. The leading lines are all good here. When doing this sort of shot you want your end subject to be a bit more dominate than you have here.     It''s a very good attempt and an even better learning shot. The dead space on the left is to over powering in the shot. Had the end pew begun at the edge it would hold far better.<br/> <br/>Exposure: Coming from a wedding photographer I know how tough it is to shoot in churches. It''s a nightmare to get a decent shot exposed correctly or even close for that matter. You have quite a bit of noise in your shot but, I really like how you compensate  by going to Sepia and giving it an antique type look. It''s funny because that is exactly what I do when I find myself in a pinch with a client and wind up with noisy shots. You did good here. Did you try B&amp;W at all? I''d like to see a B&amp;W version and maybe even introduce a tad bit more noise for effect.<br/> <br/>Overall I''d say your shot was fairly good with all things considered. Just a couple things to consider next time but you pulled it off. It''s not a snapshot and I don''t believe you finished last. Congrats and keep up the work.  I seen your port and your going to do quite well here.</td>', 'Composition; A slight shift to the right would have done a bit of good. The leading lines are all good here. When doing this sort of shot you want your end subject to be a bit more dominate than you have here.     It''s a very good attempt and an even better learning shot. The dead space on the left is to over powering in the shot. Had the end pew begun at the edge it would hold far better. Exposure: Coming from a wedding photographer I know how tough it is to shoot in churches. It''s a nightmare to get a decent shot exposed correctly or even close for that matter. You have quite a bit of noise in your shot but, I really like how you compensate  by going to Sepia and giving it an antique type look. It''s funny because that is exactly what I do when I find myself in a pinch with a client and wind up with noisy shots. You did good here. Did you try B&W at all? I''d like to see a B&W version and maybe even introduce a tad bit more noise for effect. Overall I''d say your shot was fairly good with all things considered. Just a couple things to consider next time but you pulled it off. It''s not a snapshot and I don''t believe you finished last. Congrats and keep up the work.  I seen your port and your going to do quite well here.', '2008-12-03 15:57:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5102473, 741218, 37673, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Wow, pretty cool shot you have here. As far as critique... really not much I would have personally done different. The composition is very good and I don''t see a different angle I would have chosen. The exposure is wicked. I''ve done a lot of shots similar as a photojournalist so I know the lighting is true. The only thing I would have tried and I''m not sure if you did or not would have been noise reduction?  Other than that I really can''t find anything that bothers me with this shot. Very nicely done.</td>', 'From the Critique Club Wow, pretty cool shot you have here. As far as critique... really not much I would have personally done different. The composition is very good and I don''t see a different angle I would have chosen. The exposure is wicked. I''ve done a lot of shots similar as a photojournalist so I know the lighting is true. The only thing I would have tried and I''m not sure if you did or not would have been noise reduction?  Other than that I really can''t find anything that bothers me with this shot. Very nicely done.', '2008-12-03 16:05:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5102480, 741398, 37673, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Nice bench first off.  That is totally cool.  <br/>The shot needed an different angle for sure. Maybe something much lower and a bit more to the left would have helped the composition. This shows me what I refer to as a "Flat Footed" shot. You could have changed the angle and faired much better.  The color thing is way cool. It isolates the subject and makes it literally jump out of the shot. Nice thinking there. Had you come around the left a bit and gotten lower you could have cropped a bit tighter top to bottom. Pretty cool thinking and again NICE BENCH!</td>', 'Critique Club Nice bench first off.  That is totally cool.  The shot needed an different angle for sure. Maybe something much lower and a bit more to the left would have helped the composition. This shows me what I refer to as a "Flat Footed" shot. You could have changed the angle and faired much better.  The color thing is way cool. It isolates the subject and makes it literally jump out of the shot. Nice thinking there. Had you come around the left a bit and gotten lower you could have cropped a bit tighter top to bottom. Pretty cool thinking and again NICE BENCH!', '2008-12-03 16:12:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5105868, 741369, 35994, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful view, you caught the sun rays just right. Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'What a beautiful view, you caught the sun rays just right. Congrats on the ribbon!', '2008-12-04 13:15:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5105914, 741318, 47541, '<td valign="top">When I look at a shot like this I feel inspired.  It''s not flashy, it doesn''t rely on Photoshop to process the hell out of it (like I seem to need to do often to score well on DPC), it speaks to me.<br/> <br/>A good choice of DOF and a good POV make this a great shot.  I''m not sure that I would have seen this shot as I walked by this location - that''s a talent I don''t yet have.<br/> <br/>Adding you to my fav''s.</td>', 'When I look at a shot like this I feel inspired.  It''s not flashy, it doesn''t rely on Photoshop to process the hell out of it (like I seem to need to do often to score well on DPC), it speaks to me. A good choice of DOF and a good POV make this a great shot.  I''m not sure that I would have seen this shot as I walked by this location - that''s a talent I don''t yet have. Adding you to my fav''s.', '2008-12-04 13:36:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5106679, 741277, 80096, '<td valign="top">Very unique perspective BB! I didn''t vote on this challenge nor did I enter it, but I commend you for coming up with this. <br/> <br/>I did try to capture a plaque on a park bench which was donated in behalf of a deceased person, so we must have been on the same page.</td>', 'Very unique perspective BB! I didn''t vote on this challenge nor did I enter it, but I commend you for coming up with this.  I did try to capture a plaque on a park bench which was donated in behalf of a deceased person, so we must have been on the same page.', '2008-12-04 18:32:58.000000', NULL, 0),
